M5TExVU195VTFTNGlvQXNkbElaOEt5NU53TjRDNVg5TFBvVnNYY1Q5ekhJaWp0bGFCUVZCNUF5Zw</guid><pubDate>Wed, 29 Apr 2026 19:03:09 GMT</pubDate><description>&lt;a href=\"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwgFBVV95cUxOUXdCenIzMkVXZ2RfTmktMk1EWm9IS2huY1FWY3RZRU1nbzhwTHhJRDNIbVRpV2VteVZkQzVqUG84UWQ4Q1VPME5NdWxIVGxfb0pwanpxYXdnWlRpY1RXNkFXbzU2XzZmcWNPNHhMSUVjeUtXdW16MFBrVzI4U1pmal8wR2dvM2g4eFM5TExVU195VTFTNGlvQXNkbElaOEt5NU53TjRDNVg5TFBvVnNYY1Q5ekhJaWp0bGFCUVZCNUF5Zw?oc=5\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;Powell Vs. Bitcoin: Why Crypto ETFs Trade Like Tech Stocks On Fed Day&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;font color=\"#6f6f6f\"&gt;Benzinga&lt;/font&gt;</description><source url=\"https://www.benzinga.com\">Benzinga</source></item></channel></rss>\n./crypto_news_deep_dive.json:12:    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/canada-proposes-crypto-atm-ban-over-scams-and-money-laundering\"\n./crypto_news_deep_dive.json:23:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Title: Canada proposes ban on BTC ATMs as fraud cases mount\\n\\nURL Source: https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/04/29/canada-proposes-ban-on-bitcoin-atms-as-fraud-cases-mount\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\n# Canada proposes ban on BTC ATMs as fraud cases mount\\n\\nCanada’s Liberal government has proposed a nationwide ban on bitcoin and other crypto ATMs as part of a broader effort to combat fraud and money laundering. Officials say crypto ATMs have become a “primary method” for scammers to defraud victims and for criminals to launder illicit cash, citing findings from the financial intelligence agency FINTRAC. The move comes as lawmakers also weigh banning crypto as a form of electoral donations, even though Canada hosted the world’s first bitcoin ATM in Vancouver in 2013. The measure, included in the Liberal government's Spring Economic Update released Tuesday, would eliminate crypto ATMs nationwide. Officials described the machines as a 'primary method' for defrauding victims and laundering illicit funds. 'To protect Canadians by shutting down a primary method for scammers to defraud victims, and for criminals to place their cash proceeds of crime,' the government said, it plans to prohibit the machines entirely. A crypto ATM (automated teller machine) may sound similar to a traditional cash machine that dispenses money from your bank account, but it works very differently. Instead of withdrawing cash, these machines let users convert physical cash into crypto.\\n\\nTitle: Canada Proposes Crypto ATM Ban to Tackle Scams, Money Laundering\\n\\nURL Source: https://cointelegraph.com/news/canada-proposes-crypto-atm-ban-over-scams-and-money-laundering\\n\\nPublished Time: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 10:17:25 GMT\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\nThe Canadian government has proposed banning Bitcoin and other crypto ATMs, arguing the machines have become a primary on-ramp for fraudsters and money launderers rather than a convenient access point for everyday users. The government's Spring Economic Update 2026, published on April 28, says crypto ATMs are a “primary method for scammers to defraud victims and for criminals to place their cash proceeds of crime,” and explicitly states that the government “proposes to ban crypto ATMs.” The proposal states that Canadians will still be able to buy virtual currencies from brick-and-mortar money services businesses, but the standalone kiosks that have proliferated in malls, gas stations and corner stores would be phased out. The move adds to a broader push by Ottawa to clamp down on what it frames as retail-facing crypto risks as fraud cases surge, while bringing more of the digital asset sector under tighter federal oversight. Authorities say the move is aimed at cutting off one of the most common channels used in scams that have increasingly targeted Canadians. The policy is of particular note given Canada’s early role in the sector. The world’s first publicly available Bitcoin ATM went live in a Vancouver coffee shop in 2013, making Canada the birthplace of the Bitcoin ATM. Since then, the country has grown into one of the most crypto-ATM-dense markets globally, a status regulators say has given it disproportionate exposure to fraud. Coin ATM Radar data estimates that Canada accounts for 10.1% of global crypto ATMs, second only to the United States. A months-long CBC investigation and internal Financial Transactions and Reports Analysis Centre of Canada (FINTRAC) analysis posted April 28 found that crypto ATMs have become the principal method used by domestic and foreign criminal fraudsters to extract money from Canadian scam victims and push those funds into the crypto ecosystem. Law enforcement agencies told CBC they have seen a clear uptick in cases where victims are instructed to feed cash into these machines under the guise of paying tax debts, securing romance relationships or recovering hacked accounts. The proposed ATM ban sits within a broader effort to tighten controls around high-risk corners of Canada’s crypto market while drawing core infrastructure more firmly into the regulatory perimeter. The same Spring Economic Update bolsters a new Financial Crimes Agency and gives FINTRAC more tools to refuse or revoke registrations for non-compliant money services businesses, including crypto companies.\"\n./decrypt_content.txt:3: \"@type\": \"NewsArticle\",\n./decrypt_content.txt:22: \"articleSection\": \"News\",\n./gn_redirect.txt:8:location: https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiWEFVX3lxTE5CZ0h0dW1XazZ3Q0RhYWJ1ME43NFFDZE91eGRpejd3cjJqdVd3ZzZDNi1LZWhYUzU5eVczWW9zcUcyT0dadng1TTBHcG1WU3drZ0VPN0ZDMzA?oc=5&hl=en-IN&gl=IN&ceid=IN:en\r\n./gn_redirect.txt:52:https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiWEFVX3lxTE5CZ0h0dW1XazZ3Q0RhYWJ1ME43NFFDZE91eGRpejd3cjJqdVd3ZzZDNi1LZWhYUzU5eVczWW9zcUcyT0dadng1TTBHcG1WU3drZ0VPN0ZDMzA?oc=5&hl=en-IN&gl=IN&ceid=IN:en\n./ct_article.md:3:URL Source: https://cointelegraph.com/news/judge-denies-new-trial-sam-bankman-fried\n./ct_article.md:14:Bankman-Fried in February had [requested a new trial](https://cointelegraph.com/news/sam-bankman-fried-ftx-new-trial-fraud-case) to be overseen by a different judge, making the rare move of filing a motion without consulting his lawyers and while an appeals court was considering his conviction and sentence.\n./ct_article.md:16:On Wednesday, Bankman-Fried [asked to withdraw](https://cointelegraph.com/news/sam-bankman-fried-withdraws-motion-new-trial-new-judge) his request, telling Kaplan he didn’t believe he would “get a fair hearing on this topic in front of you,” which the judge denied.\n./ct_article.md:29:_**Related:**_[_**Sam Bankman-Fried ramps up Trump support following Ellison’s release**_](https://cointelegraph.com/news/ftx-sam-bankman-fried-caroline-ellison-donald-trump)\n./ct_article.md:31:He also argued that Nishad Singh, [FTX’s former engineering lead](https://cointelegraph.com/news/ftx-nishad-singh-cftc-fine-trading-ban), who cut a plea deal with prosecutors to avoid jail and testified against Bankman-Fried at trial, [changed his testimony](https://cointelegraph.com/news/sam-bankman-fried-rule-33-new-trial-doj) “following threats from the government.”\n./ct_article.md:41:Cointelegraph is committed to independent, transparent journalism. This news article is produced in accordance with Cointelegraph’s [Editorial Policy](https://cointelegraph.com/editorial-policy) and aims to provide accurate and timely information. Readers are encouraged to verify information independently.\n./google_news.xml:1:<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\" standalone=\"yes\"?><rss version=\"2.0\" xmlns:media=\"http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/\"><channel><generator>NFE/5.0</generator><title>\"bitcoin crypto\" - Google News</title><link>https://news.google.com/search?q=bitcoin+crypto&amp;hl=en-US&amp;gl=US&amp;ceid=US:en</link><language>en-US</language><webMaster>news-webmaster@google.com</webMaster><copyright>Copyright © 2026 Google. All rights reserved. This XML feed is made available solely for the purpose of rendering Google News results within a personal feed reader for personal, non-commercial use. Any other use of the feed is expressly prohibited. By accessing this feed or using these results in any manner whatsoever, you agree to be bound by the foregoing restrictions.</copyright><lastBuildDate>Wed, 29 Apr 2026 11:16:20 GMT</lastBuildDate><image><title>Google News</title><url>https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-DR60l-K8vnyi99NZovm9HlXyZwQ85GMDxiwJWzoasZYCUrPuUM_P_4Rb7ei03j-0nRs0c4F=w256</url><link>https://news.google.com/</link><height>256</height><width>256</width></image><description>Google News</description><item><title>Institutional money is coming for bitcoin, but Adam Back says it moves slower than you think - CoinDesk</title><link>https://news.google.?oc=5</link><guid isPermaLink=\"false\">CBMi0gFBVV95cUxOVmRVMFNDb2RuLXpuOGl1dVJSd2tUWlh0VXRvX3MyWmlDaVphRDV6R2owVlNmTzA4c0dUOVBFOVBtN0cxc0FvSFpWdGhkdmhyc2Q3aWxXWDRJYTRGeV9ING91dmtBclNUNlZpTXh3UlBfdXF1REtVNi1aWWNWQ0VpN0NQeENhM3NaM01acjZvbXRiQzQwMU90LTdtNndlWHNadXBWajdnTUVwX2tMbFp4SUJXTzFrVXFWcHlQanZra0NZT3Fka2xCWm04RmxsNXJyS2c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 29 Apr 2026 04:00:47 GMT</pubDate><description>&lt;a href=\"https://news.google.?oc=5\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;Institutional money is coming for bitcoin, but Adam Back says it moves slower than you think&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;font color=\"#6f6f6f\"&gt;CoinDesk&lt;/font&gt;</description><source url=\"https://www.coindesk.com\">CoinDesk</source></item><item><title>Bitcoin and ethereum prices today, Tuesday, April 28, 2026: Values falling ahead of Fed meeting - Yahoo Finance</title><link>https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi-?oc=5</link><guid isPermaLink=\"false\">CBMi-</guid><pubDate>Tue, 28 Apr 2026 11:45:35 GMT</pubDate><description>&lt;a href=\"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi-?oc=5\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;Bitcoin and ethereum prices today, Tuesday, April 28, 2026: Values falling ahead of Fed meeting&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;font color=\"#6f6f6f\"&gt;Yahoo Finance&lt;/font&gt;</description><source