VczWW9zcUcyT0dadng1TTBHcG1WU3drZ0VPN0ZDMzA?oc=5</link><guid isPermaLink=\"false\">CBMiWEFVX3lxTE5CZ0h0dW1XazZ3Q0RhYWJ1ME43NFFDZE91eGRpejd3cjJqdVd3ZzZDNi1LZWhYUzU5eVczWW9zcUcyT0dadng1TTBHcG1WU3drZ0VPN0ZDMzA</guid><pubDate>Wed, 29 Apr 2026 04:16:02 GMT</pubDate><description>&lt;a href=\"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiWEFVX3lxTE5CZ0h0dW1XazZ3Q0RhYWJ1ME43NFFDZE91eGRpejd3cjJqdVd3ZzZDNi1LZWhYUzU5eVczWW9zcUcyT0dadng1TTBHcG1WU3drZ0VPN0ZDMzA?oc=5\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;Institutional money is coming for bitcoin, but Adam Back says it moves slower than you think&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;font color=\"#6f6f6f\"&gt;Cryptonews.net&lt;/font&gt;</description><source url=\"https://cryptonews.net\">Cryptonews.net</source></item></channel></rss>\n./cd_jina.txt:1:{\"data\":null,\"code\":451,\"name\":\"SecurityCompromiseError\",\"status\":45102,\"message\":\"Anonymous access to domain news.google.com blocked until Wed Apr 29 2026 11:35:08 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time) due to previous abuse found on https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMingFBVV95cUxOTVBaSll2bGNxbk8yM1Y1bjV3VGlUY000TVNrZ0VKQ0RYS21oUGdjWGhBbEQtSHJoWlhPd0VYWmxrV3JGLTZwbG9BYjFFR2dHbGQ0bkdwSmwwSGVtQzZpd1ZYd0NpQVVuVWNtM0tRVEZPSmY2SWIyQ2hoWFhiQmRYQ1hoUjFFYmRLLTZxam1lbEpCSURGXzNpMVFNQ3VEZw?oc=5: DDoS attack suspected: Too many domains\",\"readableMessage\":\"SecurityCompromiseError: Anonymous access to domain news.google.com blocked until Wed Apr 29 2026 11:35:08 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time) due to previous abuse found on https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMingFBVV95cUxOTVBaSll2bGNxbk8yM1Y1bjV3VGlUY000TVNrZ0VKQ0RYS21oUGdjWGhBbEQtSHJoWlhPd0VYWmxrV3JGLTZwbG9BYjFFR2dHbGQ0bkdwSmwwSGVtQzZpd1ZYd0NpQVVuVWNtM0tRVEZPSmY2SWIyQ2hoWFhiQmRYQ1hoUjFFYmRLLTZxam1lbEpCSURGXzNpMVFNQ3VEZw?oc=5: DDoS attack suspected: Too many domains\"}\n./single-topic.json:10:    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/aave-linked-defi-united-outlines-plan-to-restore-rseth-backing-after-293m-exploit\",\n./single-topic.json:22:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Title: Aave-Linked DeFi United Details rsETH Recovery Plan\\n\\nURL Source: https://cointelegraph.com/news/aave-linked-defi-united-outlines-plan-to-restore-rseth-backing-after-293m-exploit\\n\\nPublished Time: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 10:54:26 GMT\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\nThe Aave-linked recovery group DeFi United has published a technical implementation plan to restore rsETH backing after the April 18 Kelp bridge exploit released 116,500 rsETH, worth about $293 million at the time, without a corresponding burn on Unichain.\\n\\nThe plan would [convert](https://x.com/aave/status/2048958367658332413) committed Ether (ETH) into rsETH in tranches and deposit the tokens into the affected bridge lockbox, allowing the bridge to resume normal operations once the backing is restored. LayerZero and Kelp have also implemented additional security measures before the bridge returns to full operation, according to Aave.\\n\\nIn parallel, DeFi United plans to clear attacker-linked positions across Aave and Compound to recover collateral and resolve market impairments caused by the exploit. The group said seven addresses associated with the exploiter still hold active rsETH-backed positions on Aave and Compound, representing about 107,000 rsETH of the original 116,500 rsETH released in the incident.\\n\\n_**Related:**_[_**Kelp restaking platform exploited, $293M drained in attack**_](https://cointelegraph.com/news/restaking-platform-kelp-exploited-293-million)\\n\\nThe proposed sequence would temporarily adjust the rsETH oracle price to enable controlled liquidations, transfer recovered collateral to a DeFi United multisig, restore the oracle, redeem the rsETH for ETH and use the resulting funds to clear deficits across affected markets.\\n\\nThe recovery plan moves the rsETH effort from pledges and public commitments into a coordinated technical process that depends on governance approvals, temporary oracle changes and execution across several DeFi protocols. While the process is designed to restore rsETH backing, it remains contingent on DAO votes, finalized agreements and the attacker not disrupting the liquidation steps.\\n\\n![Image 1](https://resizer.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/f=auto,onerror=redirect,w=802,q=90/https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/media/file/pasted-image-17.jpeg?prefix=media%2Fcontent)\\n_Source:_[_Aave_](https://x.com/aave/status/2048958367658332413)\\n\\n## Ethereum backers joined the recovery effort\\n\\nThe technical plan follows earlier efforts to secure funding and governance support for the rsETH recovery.\\n\\nOn Monday, Consensys and Ethereum co-founder Joe Lubin [had joined DeFi United](https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-backers-commit-up-to-30000-eth-to-rseth-recovery-after-bridge-incident) with a commitment of up to 30,000 ETH, while Sharplink, a publicly traded Ethereum treasury company, joined in an advisory role to help structure the recovery plan.\\n\\n_**Related:**_[_**Crypto protocols pledge 43K ETH to restore rsETH backing**_](https://cointelegraph.com/news/defi-ecosystem-unites-and-pledges-to-rseth-relief-effort)\\n\\nOn the same day, Aave Labs [had asked the Arbitrum DAO](https://cointelegraph.com/news/arbitrum-dao-asked-to-unfreeze-30k-eth-tied-to-kelp-hacker-direct-them-to-defi-united) to release 30,765 ETH frozen by the Arbitrum Security Council [after the exploit](https://cointelegraph.com/news/arbitrum-freezes-71m-ether-connected-kelp-exploit) and send the funds to DeFi United.\\n\\n![Image 2](https://resizer.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/f=auto,onerror=redirect,w=896,q=90/https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/media/file/pasted-image-18.jpeg?prefix=media%2Fcontent)\\n_DeFi United secured over $300 million in commitments. Source: DeFi United_\\n\\nAs of Tuesday, the DeFi United website [showed](https://defiunited.world/) $302.26 million in total raised or committed toward the recovery effort, equal to 132,706.903 ETH, though some commitments remain subject to DAO votes and final execution.\\n\\n_**Magazine:**_[_**AI-driven hacks could kill DeFi — unless projects act now**_](https://cointelegraph-magazine.com/exploits-uncovered-by-ai-could-kill-defi-unless-projects-act-now/)\\n\\nCointelegraph is committed to independent, transparent journalism. This news article is produced in accordance with Cointelegraph’s [Editorial Policy](https://cointelegraph.com/editorial-policy) and aims to provide accurate and timely information. Readers are encouraged to verify information independently.\\nTitle: Aave, Compound Unveil Technical Plan to Address Fallout From $290M Kelp DAO Hack\\n\\nURL Source: https://decrypt.co/365847/aave-compound-unveil-technical-plan-to-address-fallout-from-290m-kelp-dao-hack\\n\\nPublished Time: 2026-04-28T17:36:01\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\n# Aave, Compound Unveil Technical Plan to Address Fallout From $290M Kelp DAO Hack - Decrypt\\n\\n[![Image 1: Decrypt logo](https://cdn.decrypt.co/wp-content/themes/decrypt-media/assets/images/branding-2024/full-logo-black.svg)![Image 2: Decrypt logo](https://cdn.decrypt.co/wp-content/themes/decrypt-media/assets/images/branding-2024/full-logo-white.svg)](https://decrypt.co/)[](https://decrypt.co/gg)[](https://decrypt.co/university)[](https://decrypt.co/university)[](https://decrypt.co/emerge)\\n\\n[![Image 3: Decrypt logo](https://img.decrypt.co/insecure/rs:fit:3840:0:0:0/plain/https://cdn.decrypt.co/wp-content/themes/decrypt-media/assets/images/branding-2024/logo-mark-white.svg@webp)![Image 4: Decrypt logo](https://img.decrypt.co/insecure/rs:fit:3840:0:0:0/plain/https://cdn.decrypt.co/wp-content/themes/decrypt-media/assets/images/branding-2024/logo-mark-black.svg@webp)](https://decrypt.co/)\\n\\n[News](https://decrypt.co/news)[Learn](https://decrypt.co/university)[GG](https://decrypt.co/gg)[Emerge](https://decrypt.co/emerge)[Videos](https://decrypt.co/videos)[Newsletters](https://decrypt.co/newsletters)\\n\\nEnglish\\n\\nSign Up[Partner with us](https://dastan.co/partner)\\n\\n* * *\\n\\n* * *\\n\\n[![Image 5: News](blob:http://localhost/0aa0a8ee08caf3bcc8e7e488283150b2)![Image 6: News](blob:http://localhost/9a89213175e2fb47d512c1624a349836)News](https://decrypt.co/news)[![Image 7: Predict](blob:http://localhost/83e225a6c9ce2bac8adf311c3e67de6b)![Image 8: Predict](blob:http://localhost/d3717f8b551ce4e2a9b35e1641d61392)Predict](https://myriad.markets/?utm_source=decrypt&utm_campaign=navbar)[![Image 9: AI](blob:http://localhost/62ceb084dde83843d9887bdc1213ad1f)![Image 10: AI](blob:http://localhost/7aa2f6422d5e2e5af6a262ad86bf9b91)AI](https://decrypt.co/emerge)[![Image 11: Learn](blob:http://localhost/132e5adddd21434e4b62b0d79cacaf2c)![Image 12: Learn](blob:http://localhost/132e5adddd21434e4b62b0d79cacaf2c)Learn](https://decrypt.co/university)[![Image 13: Gaming](blob:http://localhost/e44cea5a102a4ce9cbe1c97f51994f1b)![Image 14: Gaming](blob:http://localhost/f89fd6ac9ca89f35ed6d49f4a70a6652)Gaming](https://decrypt.co/gg)\\n\\n## Coin Prices\\n\\n### [BTC](https://decrypt.co/price/bitcoin)\\n\\n$77,727.00\\n\\n1.54%\\n### [ETH](https://decrypt.co/price/ethereum)\\n\\n$2,341.28\\n\\n2.55%\\n### [XRP](https://decrypt.co/price/xrp)\\n\\n$1.40\\n\\n1.12%\\n### [BNB](https://decrypt.co/price/binance-coin)\\n\\n$628.90\\n\\n0.93%\\n### [USDC](https://decrypt.co/price/usd-coin)\\n\\n$0.999869\\n\\n0.00%\\n### [SOL](https://decrypt.co/price/solana)\\n\\n$85.36\\n\\n1.96%\\n### [TRX](https://decrypt.co/price/tron)\\n\\n$0.323283\\n\\n0.03%\\n### [FIGR_HELOC](https://decrypt.co/price/figure-heloc)\\n\\n$1.033\\n\\n0.29%\\n### [DOGE](https://decrypt.co/price/dogecoin)\\n\\n$0.109735\\n\\n10.44%\\n### [WBT](https://decrypt.co/price/whitebit)\\n\\n$55.07\\n\\n1.66%\\n### [USDS](https://decrypt.co/price/usds)\\n\\n$0.999764\\n\\n-0.01%\\n### [HYPE](https://decrypt.co/price/hyperliquid)\\n\\n$40.62\\n\\n0.81%\\n### [LEO](https://decrypt.co/price/bitfinex)\\n\\n$10.36\\n\\n-0.03%\\n### [ADA](https://decrypt.co/price/cardano)\\n\\n$0.253118\\n\\n2.82%\\n#