11:    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/south-korea-s-shinhan-card-taps-solana-to-test-real-world-stablecoin-payments\"\n./final_output.json:10:    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-risks-decline-rally-speculative-not-structural-cryptoquant\",\n./final_output.json:22:URL Source: https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-risks-decline-rally-speculative-not-structural-cryptoquant\n./final_output.json:37:News\n./final_output.json:111:[Latest News](https://cointelegraph.com/category/latest-news)Published May 1, 2026\n./final_output.json:138:[News](https://decrypt.co/news)[Learn](https://decrypt.co/university)[GG](https://decrypt.co/gg)[Emerge](https://decrypt.co/emerge)[Videos](https://decrypt.co/videos)[Newsletters](https://decrypt.co/newsletters)\n./final_output.json:148:[![Image 5: News](blob:http://localhost/0aa0a8ee08caf3bcc8e7e488283150b2)![Image 6: News](blob:http://localhost/9a89213175e2fb47d512c1624a349836)News](https://decrypt.co/news)[![Image 7: Predict](blob:http://localhost/83e225a6c9ce2bac8adf311c3e67de6b)![Image 8: Predict](blob:http://localhost/d3717f8b551ce4e2a9b35e1641d61392)Predict](https://myriad.markets/?utm_source=decrypt&utm_campaign=navbar)[![Image 9: AI](blob:http://localhost/62ceb084dde83843d9887bdc1213ad1f)![Image 10: AI](blob:http://localhost/7aa2f6422d5e2e5af6a262ad86bf9b91)AI](https://decrypt.co/emerge)[![Image 11: Learn](blob:http://localhost/132e5adddd21434e4b62b0d79cacaf2c)![Image 12: Learn](blob:http://localhost/132e5adddd21434e4b62b0d79cacaf2c)Learn](https://decrypt.co/university)[![Image 13: Gaming](blob:http://localhost/e44cea5a102a4ce9cbe1c97f51994f1b)![Image 14: Gaming](blob:http://localhost/f89fd6ac9ca89f35ed6d49f4a70a6652)Gaming](https://decrypt.co/gg)\n./coindesk_article.txt:13:*   News \n./coindesk_article.txt:67:A [2023 internal analysis](https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/toronto/feeding-fraud-crypto-atm-problem-part-one-1.7647402) by Canada's financial intelligence agency, FINTRAC, found that bitcoin ATMs are likely to remain \"the primary method\" fraudsters use to collect and launder funds from victims.\n./coindesk_article.txt:94:[Latest Crypto News](https://www.coindesk.com/latest-crypto-news)\n./coindesk_article.txt:149:[Newsletters](https://www.coindesk.com/newsletters)\n./coindesk_article.txt:150:*   [CoinDesk Headlines](https://www.coindesk.com/newsletters/the-node)\n./coindesk_article.txt:151:*   [Crypto Daybook Americas](https://www.coindesk.com/newsletters/daybook-us)\n./coindesk_article.txt:152:*   [The Protocol](https://www.coindesk.com/newsletters/the-protocol)\n./coindesk_article.txt:153:*   [State of Crypto](https://www.coindesk.com/newsletters/state-of-crypto)\n./coindesk_article.txt:154:*   [Crypto for Advisors](https://www.coindesk.com/newsletters/crypto-for-advisors)\n./coindesk_article.txt:155:*   [Crypto Long & Short](https://www.coindesk.com/newsletters/crypto-long-short)\n./coindesk_article.txt:157:[News](https://www.coindesk.com/latest-crypto-news)\n./coindesk_article.txt:209:[](https://apps.apple.com/app/coindesk-crypto-bitcoin-news/id6502816903)[](https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.coindesk.mobile)\n./coindesk_article.txt:215:[](https://twitter.com/coindesk)[](https://facebook.com/coindesk)[](https://linkedin.com/company/coindesk)[](https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/)[](https://instagram.com/coindesk)[](https://www.youtube.com/coindesk)[](https://www.tiktok.com/@coindesk/)[](https://discord.com/invite/tRuUMkkQd9)[](https://t.me/CoinDeskGlobal)\n./result.json:12:    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/us-senate-bans-itself-from-prediction-markets\",\n./crypto_news.json:9:    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/sbi-seeks-to-make-bitbank-a-subsidiary-in-japan-crypto-consolidation-push\"\n./crypto_news.json:18:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Title: SBI to Make Bitbank a Subsidiary in Japan Crypto Consolidation Push\\n\\nURL Source: https://cointelegraph.com/news/sbi-seeks-to-make-bitbank-a-subsidiary-in-japan-crypto-consolidation-push\\n\\nPublished Time: Fri, 01 May 2026 11:17:45 GMT\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\nTokyo-based SBI Holdings has opened talks to acquire shares in cryptocurrency exchange Bitbank and make it a consolidated subsidiary, extending its push to consolidate regulated crypto trading platforms in Japan as the country moves toward securities-style rules for digital assets.\\n\\nThe financial conglomerate [said](https://www.sbigroup.co.jp/news/2026/0501_16298.html) Friday it is considering a share acquisition as part of a potential capital and business alliance with Bitbank. The deal remains subject to due diligence, negotiations and internal approvals, SBI said.\\n\\nThe talks come a month after SBI VC Trade [absorbed](https://www.sbivc.co.jp/newsview/umhk6419ku) Bitpoint Japan on April 1, with SBI VC Trade becoming the surviving company. A Bitbank acquisition would give SBI a larger position in Japan’s crypto exchange market at a time when policymakers are preparing to bring crypto assets under the Financial Instruments and Exchange Act.\\n\\nSBI said the potential deal would help the group establish an “overwhelming position in the domestic cryptocurrency industry,” citing Japan’s planned regulatory shift for crypto assets.\\n\\nJapan’s Cabinet approved a bill on April 10 to [amend the Financial Instruments and Exchange Act](https://cointelegraph.com/news/japan-approves-bill-classify-cryptocurrencies-financial-instruments) and the Payment Services Act, according to the Financial Services Agency. The bill is intended to strengthen market fairness, transparency and investor protection while revising rules for crypto assets.\\n\\nCrypto assets are currently regulated by the FSA under the Payment Services Act as a means of payment. The proposed changes would move crypto closer to Japan’s traditional financial market framework, with stronger disclosure, exchange oversight and rules targeting unfair trading.\\n\\nCointelegraph asked SBI Holdings for comment on the proposed Bitbank acquisition and how Japan’s shifting crypto rules are affecting the group’s exchange strategy, but had not received a response by publication.\\n\\n![Image 1](https://resizer.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/f=auto,onerror=redirect,w=896,q=90/https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/media/file/pasted-image-222.png?prefix=media%2Fcontent)\\n_Bitbank company profile. Source: SBI Group_\\n\\nBitbank is one of Japan’s major crypto exchanges. It [ranks](https://www.coingecko.com/en/exchanges/country/japan) as Japan’s leading cryptocurrency exchange by Coingecko’s trust score, which measures the legitimacy of crypto exchanges based on liquidity, trading activity, cybersecurity and operational scale.\\n\\nIt ranks third among cryptocurrency exchanges by daily trading volume, behind bitFlyer and Coincheck.\\n\\n![Image 2](https://resizer.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/f=auto,onerror=redirect,w=896,q=90/https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/media/file/pasted-image-223.png?prefix=media%2Fcontent)\\n_Top Japanese crypto exchanges by trust score. Source: Coingecko_\\n\\nThe proposed deal would add to SBI’s broader digital asset footprint. SBI made a $50 million investment in Circle's IPO in June 2025. In previous years, SBI also made strategic investments in other crypto-native companies, including BITPoint Japan, Sygnum Bank and crypto exchange TaoTao, which later merged into SBI VC Trade.\\n\\n## Japan brings crypto under TradFi umbrella, targets ETFs by 2028\\n\\nJapan’s regulatory shift comes as institutional interest in digital assets continues to grow and policymakers reassess how crypto should fit within the country’s financial markets.\\n\\nJapanese Finance Minister Satsuki Katayama first [signaled](https://cointelegraph.com/news/japan-crypto-securities-framework-exchange-led-access-2026) the intent to bring crypto under the same umbrella as traditional finance assets in January, to ensure that citizens will “benefit from digital and blockchain-based assets.”\\n\\n_**Related:**_[_**South Korea’s Shinhan Card taps Solana to test real-world stablecoin payments**_](https://cointelegraph.com/news/south-korean-credit-card-giant-partners-with-solana-for-stablecoin-payments-defi-infrastructure)\\n\\nThe country is also planning to legalize the launch of cryptocurrency exchange-traded funds (ETFs) by 2028, [according](https://cointelegraph.com/news/japan-considers-crypto-etfs-2028-nikkei) to a January report. Large financial conglomerates like SBI Holdings and Nomura are among the first companies expected to [develop crypto-linked ETFs](https://cointelegraph.com/news/sbi-plans-bitcoin-xrp-etf-japan).\\n\\n_**Magazine:**_[_**Singapore isn’t a ‘crypto hub’ — it’s something better: StraitsX CEO**_](https://cointelegraph-magazine.com/singapore-crypto-speculation-down-mas-loophole-closure-asia-express/)\\n\\nCointelegraph\"\n./article3.txt:3:URL Source: https://coinpedia.org/news/bitcoin-ethereum-and-xrp-prices-drop-as-fed-holds-rates-and-trump-rejects-iran-deal/\n./article3.txt:10:*   [Menu](https://coinpedia.org/news/bitcoin-ethereum-and-xrp-prices-drop-as-fed-holds-rates-and-trump-rejects-iran-deal/#)\n./article3.txt:12:[![Image 1: cp-logo](https://image.coinpedia.org/static/common/coinpedia-logo.svg)](https://coinpedia.org/ \"Coinpedia - Fintech & Cryptocurreny News Media| Crypto Guide\")\n./article3.txt:31:*   [![Image 15: menu-images](blob:http://localhost/e4c9fb6da3edf443a3d65e64339d7e1e)News](https://coinpedia.org/news/)\n./article3.txt:39:*   [![Image 19: menu-images](blob:http://localhost/e4c9fb6da3edf443a3d65e64339d7e1e)Markets](https://coinpedia.org/news/bitcoin-ethereum-and-xrp-prices-drop-as-fed-holds-rates-and-trump-rejects-iran-deal/#)\n./article3.txt:46:*   [![Image 21: menu-images](blob:http://localhost/e4c9fb6da3edf443a3d65e64339d7e1e)Product Reviews](https://coinpedia.org/news/bitcoin-ethereum-and-xrp-prices-drop-as-fed-holds-rates-and-trump-rejects-iran-deal/#)\n./article3.txt:53:*   [![Image 23: menu-images](blob:http://localhost/e4c9fb6da3edf443a3d65e64339d7e1e)Academy](https://coinpedia.org/news/bitcoin-ethereum-and-xrp-prices-drop-as-fed-holds-rates-and-trump-rejects-iran-deal/)\n./article3.txt:58:*   [![Image 27: menu-images](blob:http://localhost/e4c9fb6da3edf443a3d65e64339d7e1e)Find](https://coinpedia.org/news/bitcoin-ethereum-and-xrp-prices-drop-as-fed-holds-rates-and-trump-rejects-iran-deal/#)\n./article3.txt:64:*   [![Image 29: menu-images](blob:http://localhost/e4c9fb6da3edf443a3d65e64339d7e1e)Contact](https://coinpedia.org/news/bitcoin-ethereum-and-xrp-prices-drop-as-\n./crypto_news_summary.json:11:    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-risks-decline-rally-speculative-not-structural-cryptoquant\",\n./crypto_news_summary.json:22:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Title: Bitcoin Risks Decline After Futures-Driven April Rally: CryptoQuant\\n\\nURL Source: https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-risks-decline-rally-speculative-not-structural-cryptoquant\\n\\nPublished Time: Fri, 01 May 2026 10:28:12 GMT\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\n# Bitcoin risks extended retreat as April rally was futures-driven: CryptoQuant\\n\\nFutures drove up Bitcoin's price in April while spot demand declined, which CryptoQuant warned has historically preceded extended price declines.\\n\\nBitcoin could be setting up for a multimonth price decline, after a rally in April driven mainly by futures traders while spot demand declined, according to the crypto analytics firm CryptoQuant.\\n\\nBitcoin gained around 20% in April, rising from $66,000 to a peak of $79,000 in a rally “driven entirely by growth in perpetual futures demand,” CryptoQuant said in a report on Thursday.\\n\\nMeanwhile, spot demand for Bitcoin contracted throughout the rally, “indicating that the market’s marginal buyer was speculative, not fundamental,” it said.\\n\\n“The divergence between rising price and contracting spot demand is one of the clearest on-chain signals that price gains are speculative rather than structural,” CryptoQuant added.\\n\\nBitcoin is trading around $77,000 at the time of writing, rising 2.1% over the past 24 hours.\\n\\nTitle: Bitcoin Crash Incoming? April Surge Was Built on Shaky Ground, Analysts Warn\\n\\nURL Source: https://decrypt.co/366267/bitcoin-crash-incoming-april-surge-built-shaky-ground-analysts-warn\\n\\nPublished Time: 2026-04-30T20:30:19\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\n# Bitcoin Crash Incoming? April Surge Was Built on Shaky Ground, Analysts Warn - Decrypt\\n\\nThe recent surge in Bitcoin’s price, which saw it climb impressively throughout April, may not be as stable as it appears. Market analysts are pointing to underlying data that suggests the rally was built on speculative trading rather than solid, fundamental demand. Experts from analytics firm CryptoQuant have highlighted that the growth was predominantly fueled by perpetual futures contracts, a form of derivative trading that allows for high leverage. Simultaneously, on-chain data shows that actual spot-market buying—the direct purchase of Bitcoin—has been declining. This is a concerning divergence. When prices rise without the backing of genuine buying interest from long-term holders or new retail investors, it often creates a fragile market susceptible to sharp corrections. Historically, such patterns have often been the precursor to significant price drops, as the speculative fervor dies down and the lack of foundational support becomes apparent. While Bitcoin currently holds a strong position near its recent highs, investors are being warned to proceed with caution, as the shaky ground on which the April surge was built could give way, potentially leading to a market-wide crash.\"\n./cointelegraph_new.xml:2:<rss version=\"2.0\" xmlns:content=\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\" xmlns:media=\"http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xmlns:wfw=\"http://wellformedweb.org/CommentAPI/\" xmlns:atom=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom\" xmlns:sy=\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/syndication/\" xmlns:slash=\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/slash/\">\n./cointelegraph_new.xml:4:    <title>Cointelegraph.com News</title>\n./cointelegraph_new.xml:6:    <atom:link href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/rss?_refresh=nm5ymi&amp;cachebust=true\" rel=\"self\" type=\"application/rss+xml\"/>\n./cointelegraph_new.xml:7:    <description>Cointelegraph covers fintech, blockchain and Bitcoin bringing you the latest crypto news and analyses on the future of money.</description>\n./cointelegraph_new.xml:14:      <title>Cointelegraph.com News</title>\n./cointelegraph_new.xml:17:      <description>Cointelegraph covers fintech, blockchain and Bitcoin bringing you the latest crypto news and analyses on the future of money.</description>\n./cointelegraph_new.xml:22:      <atom:updated>Wed, 29 Apr 2026 10:10:18 +0000</atom:updated>\n./cointelegraph_new.xml:23:      <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://cointelegraph.com/news/celsius-founder-settlement-includes-10m-payment-suspended-47b-judgment</guid>\n./cointelegraph_new.xml:24:      <link><![CDATA[https://cointelegraph.com/news/celsius-founder-settlement-includes-10m-payment-suspended-47b-judgment?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound]]></link>\n./cointelegraph_new.xml:29:      <category>Latest News</category>\n./cointelegraph_new.xml:34:      <atom:updated>Wed, 29 Apr 2026 09:49:45 +0000</atom:updated>\n./cointelegraph_new.xml:35:      <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://cointelegraph.com/news/canada-proposes-crypto-atm-ban-over-scams-and-money-laundering</guid>\n./cointelegraph_new.xml:36:      <link><![CDATA[https://cointelegraph.com/news/canada-proposes-crypto-atm-ban-over-scams-and-money-laundering?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound]]></link>\n./cointelegraph_new.xml:41:      <category>Latest News</category>\n./cointelegraph_new.xml:46:      <atom:updated>Wed, 29 Apr 2026 09:19:21 +0000</atom:updated>\n./cointelegraph_new.xml:48:      <link><![CDATA[https://coint