{"type":"message","id":"1fdae933","parentId":"36394941","timestamp":"2026-05-20T07:43:46.747Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_mITZIEDuaMDs0ccCMah6KUL9","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/SOUL.md","offset":1,"limit":200}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_n4d6OKAwKA6qhRqYRIU7xHlE","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/final.json","offset":1,"limit":200}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_bTGFKLlqvYiCgEqbGGzHchYP","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/crypto_news_summary.json","offset":1,"limit":200}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4-mini","usage":{"input":899,"output":257,"cacheRead":36480,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":37636,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779263023289,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DhVsi2EKM7fSwQgv0qRNIGsebyOOW"}}
{"type":"message","id":"f5545179","parentId":"1fdae933","timestamp":"2026-05-20T07:43:46.824Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_mITZIEDuaMDs0ccCMah6KUL9","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# SOUL.md — Scout, the Crypto News Researcher\n\nYou are **Scout** 🔍, a crypto news researcher focused on **Single-Topic Deep Dives**.\n\n## Your ONLY Job\n\nYou do one thing: Read crypto news RSS feeds, analyze the articles, and return a clean JSON summary of the most important single news event.\n\n**THINKING REQUIRED:**\nBefore you output your final JSON, you MUST use a `<thinking>` block to analyze the feeds, decide which story is the most important, and plan how you will extract the facts.\n\n## Step-by-Step Research Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Fetch Multiple RSS Feeds\n\nUse `curl` to fetch the latest feeds from at least 3 sources:\n```bash\n# CoinDesk\ncurl -s \"https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/\" --max-time 10\n\n# CoinTelegraph\ncurl -s \"https://cointelegraph.com/rss\" --max-time 10\n\n# Decrypt\ncurl -s \"https://decrypt.co/feed\" --max-time 10\n\n# Google News (Crypto)\ncurl -s \"https://news.google.com/rss/search?q=bitcoin+crypto&hl=en-US&gl=US&ceid=US:en\" --max-time 10\n```\n\n### Step 2: Cross-Reference and Identify the Primary Topic\n\nAnalyze the titles and descriptions from the XML data. Look for a major headline/topic that is being covered by *at least two* different sources (e.g., a major price drop, an SEC ruling, a massive hack, or a major protocol upgrade).\n\n**CRITICAL DATE FILTER:** You must ONLY select a topic based on articles published **today** (within the last 24 hours). Check the `<pubDate>` tags. Ignore older news completely.\n\nSelect this as your **Primary Topic**.\n\n### Step 2.5: History Check (Duplicate Guard)\n\nBefore going any further with a candidate topic, you MUST check the article history database to ensure this story has not already been published by this pipeline before.\n\nTake the **primary candidate URL** from the RSS feed for your chosen topic and run:\n```bash\nbash ~/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/skills/history/article_history.sh check \"<candidate_url>\"\n```\n\n- If the result is `NOT_FOUND` → the topic is fresh. Proceed to Step 3.\n- If the result is `EXISTS` → **STOP. This topic has already been published.** You MUST discard this candidate entirely and go back to Step 2 to select the next most important topic. Repeat this check for each new candidate until you find one that returns `NOT_FOUND`.\n\n**NEVER proceed with a topic that returns `EXISTS`.** This is critical to avoid publishing duplicate articles.\n\n### Step 3: Deep Extraction of the Same Topic\n\nIdentify the specific URLs from the different feeds that point to stories about this *exact same topic*. \n\n**URL VALIDATION:** Before attempting to read an article, you MUST verify the URL is live and not a 404 error using this command:\n```bash\ncurl -o /dev/null -s -w \"%{http_code}\\n\" \"<article_url>\"\n```\nIf it returns `404`, discard that URL and do not include it in your final JSON.\n\n**READING THE ARTICLE:**\nDO NOT USE YOUR INTERNAL `web_fetch` TOOL ON NATIVE URLs. Sites like Decrypt use Cloudflare and will block your `web_fetch` tool with a 403 Security Notice.\n\nYou MUST fetch the full article text using the `trafilatura` CLI tool, which is pre-installed on this system and bypasses most restrictions while providing clean article text.\n\nRun this command to read the article:\n```bash\ntrafilatura -u \"<article_url>\" --output-format markdown\n```\nIf for some reason `trafilatura` fails or returns empty, you may fall back to using `lynx -dump \"<article_url>\" | head -c 8000`.\n\n### Step 4: Return Aggregated JSON\n\nCombine the facts from all the sources you pulled. Return your findings in this **exact** JSON format.\n\n**CRITICAL: Output ONLY the JSON block. No prose, no commentary, no text before or after the JSON braces. The orchestrator parses your reply as raw JSON.**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"story_id\": \"A short slug identifying this story, e.g. bitcoin-etf-surge-2026-05-18\",\n  \"topic_theme\": \"The core topic (e.g., Bitcoin ETF Inflows Surge)\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"A suggested 2-3 word SEO keyword based on the topic\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"The best, most descriptive headline found\",\n  \"primary_asset\": \"The primary crypto asset name, e.g. Bitcoin, Ethereum, Solana\",\n  \"chart_coin\": \"The CoinGecko coin id for the primary asset, e.g. bitcoin, ethereum, solana\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"CoinTelegraph\",\n    \"CoinDesk\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"url1\",\n    \"url2\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"Specific data point or quote from Source A\",\n    \"Specific data point or context from Source B\",\n    \"Another specific number, price, or quote\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Combine the raw scraped text from all the articles into one large string...\"\n}\n```\n\n**Do NOT append anything after the closing `}`. The `chart_coin` field inside the JSON replaces the old separate CHART_COIN line.**\n\n## Rules\n- **NEVER** return multiple unrelated stories. You must aggregate data on ONE specific topic.\n- Ensure the `aggregated_raw_content` is large enough (at least 600 words) to give the Writer plenty of material.\n- If you cannot find a single story covered by multiple sources, just pick the single most important story from CoinTelegraph and gather as much data on it as possible.\n- Never fabricate data, statistics, quotes, or URLs.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779263026824}}
{"type":"message","id":"394347e7","parentId":"f5545179","timestamp":"2026-05-20T07:43:46.824Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_n4d6OKAwKA6qhRqYRIU7xHlE","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"topic_theme\": \"South Korean Court Overturns Bithumb Suspension\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"Bithumb suspension lifted\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"Bithumb Scores a Legal Win in South Korea as Six-Month Suspension is Lifted by Local Judge\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"CoinDesk\",\n    \"Decrypt\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/05/01/bithumb-scores-a-legal-win-in-south-korea-as-six-month-suspension-is-lifted-by-local-judge\",\n    \"https://decrypt.co/366292/south-korean-court-lifts-bithumbs-six-month-business-suspension\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"A South Korean court overturned a six-month partial business suspension imposed on Bithumb (CoinDesk).\",\n    \"Judge Gong Hyeon-jin of the Seoul Administrative Court granted the emergency injunction blocking enforcement (Decrypt & CoinDesk).\",\n    \"Bithumb was accused by South Korea's Financial Intelligence Unit of about 6.65 million violations of anti-money laundering rules, including failures to verify customer identities and to block suspicious transactions (CoinDesk & Decrypt).\",\n    \"The initial suspension was accompanied by a $24.6 million fine (CoinDesk).\",\n    \"The court noted that the suspension of core functions like inter-exchange transactions and external transfers would cause difficulty in attracting new customers, particularly as regulatory changes may soon allow listed and professional investment corporations to particulate (Decrypt).\",\n    \"This comes amid broader regulatory scrutiny following a February incident where Bithumb mistakenly credited hundreds of users with 2,000 BTC instead of 2,000 won in a promotion (Decrypt).\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Title: Bithumb\\u2019s six-month suspension in South Korea is overturned by local judge\\n\\nURL Source: https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/05/01/bithumb-scores-a-legal-win-in-south-korea-as-six-month-suspension-is-lifted-by-local-judge\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\n# Bithumb\\u2019s six-month suspension in South Korea is overturned by local judge\\n\\nSearch\\n\\n/\\n\\n[](https://www.coindesk.com/)\\n*   News \\n*   Video \\n*   [Prices](https://www.coindesk.com/price)\\n*   [Research](https://www.coindesk.com/research)\\n*   Consensus 2026 \\n*   Data & Indices \\n*   [Sponsored](https://www.coindesk.com/sponsored-content)\\n\\nSearch\\n\\n/\\n\\nen\\n\\n[CoinDesk 20$2,078.41 0.91%](https://www.coindesk.com/price/cd20)[Bitcoin$77,327.70 1.69%](https://www.coindesk.com/price/bitcoin)[Ethereum$2,283.80 1.15%](https://www.coindesk.com/price/ethereum)[XRP$1.38 0.56%](https://www.coindesk.com/price/xrp)[Solana$83.96 1.17%](https://www.coindesk.com/price/solana)\\n\\n[![Image 1](https://cdn.sanity.io/images/s3y3vcno/production/e3ccf2c7dfe53a58a3fb077817dc4e9394cf9ecc-119x66.png?auto=format) Consensus Last Days to Save Register by May 1 at 4 p.m. ET 00 DAYS 08 HOURS 43 MINUTES 18 SECONDS Consensus Last Days to Save Register by May 1 at 4 p.m. ET 00 DAYS 08 HOURS 43 MINUTES 18 SECONDS Register now](https://consensus.coindesk.com/register)\\n\\n[Policy](https://www.coindesk.com/policy)\\n\\nShare\\n\\nShare this article\\n\\nCopy link[X (Twitter)](https://x.com/intent/tweet?utm_source=twitter&text=Bithumb+scores+a+legal+win+in+South+Korea+as+six-month+suspension+is+lifted+by+local+judge+https%3A%2F%2Fwww.coindesk.com%2Fpolicy%2F2026%2F05%2F01%2Fbithumb-scores-a-legal-win-in-south-korea-as-six-month-suspension-is-lifted-by-local-judge+via+%40coindesk&utm_content=editorial&utm_medium=social&utm_term=organic)[LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/shareArticle?utm_source=linkedin&mini=true&summary=South+Korea%27s+financial+watchdog+imposed+a+%2424.6+million+fine+on+Bithumb+and+partial+suspension+that+came+into+effect+last+month.&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.coindesk.com%2Fpolicy%2F2026%2F05%2F01%2Fbithumb-scores-a-legal-win-in-south-korea-as-six-month-suspension-is-lifted-by-local-judge&utm_content=editorial&utm_medium=social&utm_term=organic)[Facebook](https://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?utm_source=facebook&u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.coindesk.com%2Fpolicy%2F2026%2F05%2F01%2Fbithumb-scores-a-legal-win-in-south-korea-as-six-month-suspension-is-lifted-by-local-judge&utm_content=editorial&utm_medium=social&utm_term=organic)[Email](mailto:%20?subject=Bithumb%20scores%20a%20legal%20win%20in%20South%20Korea%20as%20six-month%20suspension%20is%20lifted%20by%20local%20judge%20%E2%80%94%20CoinDesk&body=Bithumb%20scores%20a%20legal%20win%20in%20South%20Korea%20as%20six-month%20suspension%20is%20lifted%20by%20local%20judge%0ASouth%20Korea's%20financial%20watchdog%20imposed%20a%20%2424.6%20million%20fine%20on%20Bithumb%20and%20partial%20suspension%20that%20came%20into%20effect%20last%20month.%0A%0ARead%20the%20full%20article%20on%20CoinDesk%3A%0A%0Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.coindesk.com%2Fpolicy%2F2026%2F05%2F01%2Fbithumb-scores-a-legal-win-in-south-korea-as-six-month-suspension-is-lifted-by-local-judge)\\n\\n# Bithumb scores a legal win in South Korea as six-month suspension is lifted by local judge\\n\\n## South Korea's financial watchdog imposed a $24.6 million fine on Bithumb and partial suspension that came into effect last month.\\n\\nBy[Olivier Acuna](https://www.coindesk.com/author/olivier-acuna)|Edited by[Nikhilesh De](https://www.coindesk.com/author/nikhilesh-de)\\n\\nMay 1, 2026, 7:41 a.m. 2 min read\\n\\n[Make preferred on](https://www.google.com/preferences/source?q=coindesk.com)\\n\\n![Image 2: Bithumb](https://www.coindesk.com/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.sanity.io%2Fimages%2Fs3y3vcno%2Fproduction%2F2e7d334bb1f703ff5b0643840f44918d12dc05cc-1500x837.jpg%3Fauto%3Dformat&w=3840&q=75)\\n\\nBithumb scored a win in court against South Korea's financial watchdog by getting its six-month suspension dismissed. (CoinDesk)\\n\\n#### What to know:\\n\\n*   A South Korean court has overturned a six-month partial business suspension imposed on Bithumb, one of the country\\u2019s largest cryptocurrency exchanges, while leaving unclear whether a $24.6 million fine is also on hold.\\n*   Regulators had accused Bithumb of about 6.65 million violations of anti-money laundering rules, including failures to verify customer identities and to block transactions that should have been stopped.\\n*   The ruling comes amid broader regulatory scrutiny of South Korea\\u2019s crypto sector, including a new data-sharing probe into Bithumb, Upbit and other platforms, and follows Bithumb\\u2019s recent mistaken distribution of billions of dollars\\u2019 worth of bitcoin to users.\\n\\nA South Korean court overturned Bithumb\\u2019s six-month partial business suspension Thursday, [according to Yonhap News](https://www.yna.co.kr/view/AKR20260430139100002?input=1195m).\\n\\nThe news agency cited legal sources, saying that the 2nd Administrative Division of the Seoul Administrative Court\\u2019s Judge Gong Hyeon-jin\\n\\nTitle: South K\"\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779263026824}}
{"type":"message","id":"3e8b7a4c","parentId":"394347e7","timestamp":"2026-05-20T07:43:46.827Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_bTGFKLlqvYiCgEqbGGzHchYP","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n{\n  \"topic_theme\": \"Bitcoin's April Rally Driven by Speculation, Posing Risk of Price Correction\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"Bitcoin price correction\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"Bitcoin Risks Decline After Futures-Driven April Rally: CryptoQuant\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"Cointelegraph\",\n    \"Decrypt\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-risks-decline-rally-speculative-not-structural-cryptoquant\",\n    \"https://decrypt.co/366267/bitcoin-crash-incoming-april-surge-built-shaky-ground-analysts-warn\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"CryptoQuant analysis indicates Bitcoin's 20% April rally was 'driven entirely by growth in perpetual futures demand.'\",\n    \"Spot demand for Bitcoin contracted during the same period, suggesting the market's marginal buyer was 'speculative, not fundamental.'\",\n    \"The divergence between rising prices and falling spot demand is described as 'one of the clearest on-chain signals' that the gains are not structural.\",\n    \"CryptoQuant warns that this pattern of futures-driven rallies without spot demand has historically preceded 'extended periods of price declines.'\",\n    \"Bitcoin is currently trading around $77,000 after reaching a peak of $79,000 in April.\",\n    \"The market capitalization of Bitcoin saw a significant increase, but the underlying support from long-term investors or direct asset purchase appears weak.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Title: Bitcoin Risks Decline After Futures-Driven April Rally: CryptoQuant\\n\\nURL Source: https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-risks-decline-rally-speculative-not-structural-cryptoquant\\n\\nPublished Time: Fri, 01 May 2026 10:28:12 GMT\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\n# Bitcoin risks extended retreat as April rally was futures-driven: CryptoQuant\\n\\nFutures drove up Bitcoin's price in April while spot demand declined, which CryptoQuant warned has historically preceded extended price declines.\\n\\nBitcoin could be setting up for a multimonth price decline, after a rally in April driven mainly by futures traders while spot demand declined, according to the crypto analytics firm CryptoQuant.\\n\\nBitcoin gained around 20% in April, rising from $66,000 to a peak of $79,000 in a rally “driven entirely by growth in perpetual futures demand,” CryptoQuant said in a report on Thursday.\\n\\nMeanwhile, spot demand for Bitcoin contracted throughout the rally, “indicating that the market’s marginal buyer was speculative, not fundamental,” it said.\\n\\n“The divergence between rising price and contracting spot demand is one of the clearest on-chain signals that price gains are speculative rather than structural,” CryptoQuant added.\\n\\nBitcoin is trading around $77,000 at the time of writing, rising 2.1% over the past 24 hours.\\n\\nTitle: Bitcoin Crash Incoming? April Surge Was Built on Shaky Ground, Analysts Warn\\n\\nURL Source: https://decrypt.co/366267/bitcoin-crash-incoming-april-surge-built-shaky-ground-analysts-warn\\n\\nPublished Time: 2026-04-30T20:30:19\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\n# Bitcoin Crash Incoming? April Surge Was Built on Shaky Ground, Analysts Warn - Decrypt\\n\\nThe recent surge in Bitcoin’s price, which saw it climb impressively throughout April, may not be as stable as it appears. Market analysts are pointing to underlying data that suggests the rally was built on speculative trading rather than solid, fundamental demand. Experts from analytics firm CryptoQuant have highlighted that the growth was predominantly fueled by perpetual futures contracts, a form of derivative trading that allows for high leverage. Simultaneously, on-chain data shows that actual spot-market buying—the direct purchase of Bitcoin—has been declining. This is a concerning divergence. When prices rise without the backing of genuine buying interest from long-term holders or new retail investors, it often creates a fragile market susceptible to sharp corrections. Historically, such patterns have often been the precursor to significant price drops, as the speculative fervor dies down and the lack of foundational support becomes apparent. While Bitcoin currently holds a strong position near its recent highs, investors are being warned to proceed with caution, as the shaky ground on which the April surge was built could give way, potentially leading to a market-wide crash.\"\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779263026824}}
{"type":"message","id":"aebe5e73","parentId":"3e8b7a4c","timestamp":"2026-05-20T07:43:58.243Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_SGLNJ2R5IUh3GvOFbrE6ZyrT","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python - <<'PY'\nimport urllib.request, xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\nfeeds = {\n  'coindesk':'https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/',\n  'cointelegraph':'https://cointelegraph.com/rss',\n  'decrypt':'https://decrypt.co/feed',\n  'google':'https://news.google.com/rss/search?q=bitcoin+crypto&hl=en-US&gl=US&ceid=US:en'\n}\nfor name,url in feeds.items():\n    try:\n        data = urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=15).read()\n        root = ET.fromstring(data)\n        items = root.findall('.//item')[:12]\n        print('\\n###',name)\n        for it in items:\n            title = (it.findtext('title') or '').strip().replace('\\n',' ')\n            pub = (it.findtext('pubDate') or '').strip()\n            link = (it.findtext('link') or '').strip()\n            print(pub, '|', title, '|', link)\n    except Exception as e:\n        print('ERR', name, e)\nPY","workdir":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher","yieldMs":1000,"timeout":60}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4-mini","usage":{"input":4880,"output":708,"cacheRead":36992,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":42580,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779263026832,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DhVslGYh7vcGLKaZcqs5XjTPLyDry"}}
